<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Parameter page</title>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag 'parameter' %>
  <head>
  <body>
    <%= yield %>
  </body>
</html>

<div class = "homescreen">
<header>
<a href="https://genome.duke.edu/">
  <%= image_tag 'logo.png', alt: 'Duke Logo' %>
</a>
<h2 style = "color:white;" >THE SCHMID LAB MICROBIAL GROWTH MODEL</h2>
<nav>
  <a class = "wel_nav" href="/help" >HELP</a>
  <a class = "wel_nav" href="/resources">RESOURCES</a>
  <a class = "wel_nav" href="/admin">ADMIN</a>
</nav>
</header>


  <div class="column skinny">
    <% content_for :title, "Parameters page" %>

    <style>
      .radio-container {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        margin: auto;
      }

      .radio-container label {
        margin-right: 10px;
      }

      .dropdown-container {
        display: none;
      }
    </style>

    <script>
      function toggleDropdown() {
        var dropdown = document.getElementById("pool-options-dropdown");
        var checkbox = document.getElementById("pool-replicates-yes");
        var dropdownHeader = document.getElementById("dropdown-header");
      
        dropdown.style.display = checkbox.checked ? "block" : "none";
        dropdownHeader.textContent = checkbox.checked ? "Pool on: (select at least one)" : "";
      }
    </script>

  <h1>Select Options</h1>
  
  <p>The Schmid Lab Growth Model can make use of several different optional parameters to optimize your results. Below, please select from these options before proceeding to the next page.</p>
  <div class="general-white-block">
    <form action="/next_step" method="post">
      <h2>Pool Replicates?</h2>

      <div class="radio-container">
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="pool_replicates" value="no" checked>
          No
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="pool_replicates" value="yes" id="pool-replicates-yes" onclick="toggleDropdown()">
          Yes
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="pooling-para"> Please select the variable to pool on. 
      If selecting multiple variables, the Schmid Lab Growth Model will pool based on all unique combinations of the selected variables and model them jointly. 
      For more information on this process, please <a href="http://firasmidani.github.io/amiga/doc/pooling.html">click here</a>.
      </div>
      <div class="dropdown-container" id="pool-options-dropdown">
        <h3 id="dropdown-header"></h3>
        <select name="pool_options" multiple>
          <option value="Plate_ID">Plate ID</option>
          <option value="Isolate">Isolate</option>
          <option value="PM">PM</option>
          <option value="Replicate">Replicate</option>
          <option value="Substrate">Substrate</option>
          <option value="Group">Group</option>
          <option value="Control">Control</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <input type="submit" value="Next">
    </form>
    </div>
  